From: OpenWrt MT6990 repair <mt6990@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: do not run fallback poll on MT6990

The fallback delayed worker is independent of phylink_pcs.poll. On MT6990
the forced PCS status does not expose BMSR_LSTATUS, so this worker resets and
reconfigures the analog SerDes every second forever. MT6990 has a fixed
2500base-x link and must not start this recovery worker.

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -487,8 +487,9 @@ static int mtk_pcs_lynxi_enable(struct p
 	}
 
 	if (mpcs->xfi_tphy) {
 		phy_power_on(mpcs->xfi_tphy);
-		schedule_delayed_work(&mpcs->link_poll, HZ);
+		if (!(mpcs->flags & MTK_SGMII_FLAG_MT6990))
+			schedule_delayed_work(&mpcs->link_poll, HZ);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
